exports[`preserves the readable workspace layout across class, library, student, detail, picker and editor states > new skill editor 1`] = `
"<section class="skills-workspace" aria-busy="false"><p class="skills-notice" role="status">Selection saved for new sessions.</p><section class="skills-editor" data-dirty="true"><header class="skills-toolbar"><button type="button">Back</button><span role="status">Draft kept in this tab</span></header><h2>New skill</h2><details class="skills-guide"><summary>How to write a skill</summary><p>The header between --- identifies the skill: name, description and optional metadata.title. Write the complete Markdown instructions below it.</p><p>Like Testing: explain what the learner should master and in what order, exercises in their project, questions and scaffolding, what not to solve for them, and evidence of understanding.</p><p>In didactic skills, criterios is optional: each entry has codigo and enunciado; optional niveles contains exactly four progress descriptions. Keep supplied curriculum codes; use local codes for your own criteria.</p><p>name is an identifier of up to 64 lowercase letters, digits and hyphens. Choose it when creating; change metadata.title to rename a saved skill.</p></details><details class="skills-generation"><summary>Help me draft it</summary><label>What should students learn, and what are your criteria?<textarea rows="4" maxLength="16000"></textarea></label><button type="button" disabled="">Generate draft</button><p>Uses the model configured for this class. Generated text awaits your review.</p></details><form><fieldset><label for="skill-markdown">SKILL.md</label><textarea id="skill-markdown" class="skills-markdown" rows="26" spellCheck="false" aria-invalid="false" aria-describedby="skill-markdown-error">---
name: skill-11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111
description: &#x27;&#x27;
metadata:
  title: &#x27;&#x27;
# Completa la descripción y el título. Conserva name al editar una skill existente.
# Opcional: criterios con codigo, enunciado y exactamente cuatro niveles.
# criterios:
#   - codigo: local-1
#     enunciado: Qué debe demostrar el alumno
#     niveles: [Con guía, Con ayuda puntual, De forma autónoma, En situaciones nuevas]
---

# Lo que tiene que dominar

&lt;!-- Objetivos y progresión del aprendizaje. --&gt;

## Cómo plantear el ejercicio

&lt;!-- Situación, preguntas y ayudas. --&gt;

## Qué no hacer

&lt;!-- Decisiones que debe tomar el alumno. --&gt;

## Cómo saber si lo ha entendido

&lt;!-- Evidencias observables y respuesta a las dificultades. --&gt;
</textarea><p id="skill-markdown-error" class="skills-field-error" role="alert"> </p></fieldset><div class="skills-secondary"><button type="button">Preview</button><button type="button">Discard draft</button></div><footer class="skills-save-bar"><div><p>Not assigned yet.</p><small>Changes apply to new sessions. Conversations in progress keep their content.</small></div><button type="submit" class="skills-primary">Save to library</button></footer></form></section></section>"
`;

